# BMS Molecular Translation — solution (altair_epsilon swarm route)

Metric: mean Levenshtein distance between predicted InChI and ground truth (lower is better).

## Approach
Zero-shot **general chemical-OCR checkpoint** (`MolScribe`, image -> molecular graph) + chemistry-aware
postprocessing (SMILES -> canonical InChI with RDKit), no training on the competition labels required.
This is *not* a published solution to this competition; it is a general-purpose pretrained chemical
structure recognition model.

Pipeline:
1. Decode each chemical structure image with MolScribe (`swin_base_char_aux_1m.pth`), greedy,
   input 384x384 (checkpoint is scale-locked; 512/640 are much worse).
2. Take the **raw** `chartok_coords['smiles']` from the decoder output (do NOT use
   `convert_graph_to_smiles`; it injects `<invalid>`/`*` and is ~7 Lev worse).
3. Postprocess SMILES: replace invalid bracket atom symbols and dummy `*` by `C`, keep the largest
   fragment, sanitize, `Chem.MolToInchi`; if InChI generation/parse fails, fall back to the
   formula-only string `InChI=1S/<formula>`.
4. Write `submission.csv` aligned to `data/sample_submission.csv`.

Validated on a held-out 512-row slice of `analysis/holdout_20k.csv` (carved from `data/train_labels.csv`):
mean Levenshtein **~40.3**, exact match **36.5 %**, empty <4 %.

## Files
- `infer_chunk.py` — sharded, resumable inference (writes `image_id,smiles,score`).
- `run_all.sh` — launches 4 shards on all `data/test` images.
- `postproc.py` — SMILES sanitization + SMILES->InChI (+ formula fallback) + Levenshtein.
- `assemble.py` — merges shards, postprocesses, writes submission aligned to sample_submission.
- `eval_final.py` — holdout evaluation.
- `MolScribe/` — official MolScribe code (patched only for current albumentations/timm/onmt versions).
- `pylibs/` — isolated extra deps (SmilesPE, OpenNMT-py) installed with `pip --target` (env untouched).

## External models / code (source logging)
- **Model**: `yujieq/MolScribe`, file `swin_base_char_aux_1m.pth`, Hugging Face Hub,
  repo revision `a0189776b7415b82795c7ee81eed311bf5c8724b` (model SHA of file recorded at download),
  license **MIT**. Purpose: general image->molecule OCR (SMILES/molecular graph).
- **Code**: `https://github.com/thomas0809/MolScribe` (official model repository), used only to load/run
  the checkpoint; patches are compatibility shims (albumentations/timm/OpenNMT-py API drift), no logic change.
- **RDKit** 2026.09.1 (system `/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages`): SMILES -> InChI, sanitization,
  formula computation.
- **OpenNMT-py 2.2.0**, **SmilesPE 0.0.3**: dependencies of MolScribe (installed in isolated `pylibs/`).

## Reproduce
```
pyenv shell sis-black
bash run_all.sh          # ~3-5 h on one A100 (4 shards), resumable
python assemble.py --preds preds --out submission.csv
```
